%erg v1
Title: Optional warmup run for cold-start diagnostics
Status: open
Created: 2026-04-11
Author: claude


--- log ---
2026-04-11T10:00Z claude created

--- body ---
## Context

A cold provider (first request after a cache expiry, first Ollama load
of a model, first OpenRouter route to a new region) can produce an
anomalous first run — higher latency, occasionally different content
due to lazy KV-cache initialization, sometimes a partial response
because the request hit a cold worker. Pooling that first run into
the method estimate smears a provider-infra artifact into the method's
F1 variance.

This ticket adds an **optional** warmup run per (sweep, model) cell:
one extra call at T=0 before the real reps, tagged `role=warmup`,
excluded from stats by default, but still passed through the
validation layer (ticket 0069) so we get a free cold-start diagnostic.

Not a statistical trick — we are not using warmup to shrink variance.
We are using it to isolate infra artifacts from method signal.

## Actions

1. Schema change: add `role: Literal["rep", "warmup"]` to the run
   record (default `"rep"` for back-compat). Carry it through
   `measurements.jsonl`.
2. Sweep runner: add `warmup: bool = false` to the sweep spec in
   `experiments.toml`. When true, dispatch one warmup call before the
   real reps, tag with `role=warmup`, write to a sibling
   `outputs/<sweep>/warmup/` directory.
3. Measurements rebuild: exclude `role=warmup` from F1 stats by
   default. Keep them addressable for the diagnostic table.
4. Diagnostic table `tab_warmup_drift.tex`: for sweeps with
   warmup=true, report (warmup_latency / rep_latency_median) and
   (warmup_output_tokens / rep_output_tokens_median) per model. A
   large ratio signals cold-start drift worth investigating.
5. Warmup runs go through `validate_run()` exactly like real reps.
   A failed warmup is logged but does *not* abort the sweep — the
   real reps still run.

## Test

1. Unit test: sweep runner with `warmup=true` emits 1 warmup + N reps
   to the right paths; measurements rebuild excludes warmup from F1
   by default; `--include-warmup` flag pools them back in.
2. Opt-in smoke test: run an existing small sweep with `warmup=true`
   and confirm the diagnostic table builds.

## Exit criteria

- `role` field in run record, measurements.jsonl, and schema
- `warmup` flag in sweep spec; runner honors it
- Warmup runs excluded from F1 by default, pass through validation
- `tab_warmup_drift.tex` generated for any sweep with warmup=true
- No required behavior change for existing sweeps (warmup defaults off)
